  era: "1793 \xB7 Section 20 \xB7 East India Company Rule \xB7 1765 \u2013 1858"
  title: Permanent Settlement
  text: Introduced by Cornwallis in 1793 in Bengal, Bihar and Orissa, the Permanent Settlement made zamindars owners of the land, with revenue fixed forever. It ensured a steady income but left peasants at the mercy of zamindars.
